WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:25.210
Galar Region

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.980
The Pokémon in Sakuragi Park
are as lively as ever.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.740
Everybody! Chow time!

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:02.740
Okay, I get the message!

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.350
Here, Sarunori.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.560
Oh, Raichu, you’re helping out?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.520
Easy does it, Sarunori.
Wait your turn.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.850
Lined up like that,
they almost look like a Tairetsu.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.390
Tairetsu?

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:33.650
Tairetsu are Pokémon
that always work together in groups of six.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:36.590
Huh...
So it’s like a Tamatama?

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.690
You got it.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.900
The six have perfect teamwork,
so they act like one Pokémon!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.760
What?! I wanna see that!

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.280
You’ll have to go
to the Galar Region, then.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.800
The Galar Region...!

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.260
We’ve gotta go, yeah?

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.210
You bet!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.790
They should be around here...

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:32.790
Let’s see...

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.010
A Monster Ball?

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.170
What’s it doing here?

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:42.920
What’s wrong?

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.290
Nothing...

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.210
I thought it was a Monster Ball,
but it’s a Pokémon...

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.670
Is that a Maggyo?!

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:57.870
Maggyo! Galarian Form! Trap Pokémon!
Ground/Steel type!

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:01.790
It lures prey in with its conspicuous lips
as it lies in wait in the mud!

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:05.570
It clamps down on them
with its jagged steel fins!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.820
Monster Ball, go!

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:21.840
Maggyo: Galarian Form’s data
will be added to the Index!

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:24.200
I caught a Maggyo!

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:28.250
Let’s keep going!
Tairetsu must be around here too!

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.440
Let’s find it!

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.060
Yeah!

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.950
Okay, mix au lait flavor?

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.690
Hold on there just one minute.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:49.590
Oh, there it is!

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.550
Tairetsu! Formation Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:06.610
One is the captain,
and the other five are the troopers!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.140
The captain’s orders are absolute!

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.030
So the one at the front
is the captain...

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.480
He was right...
They’re in perfect sync!

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.370
They’re battling over there!

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:43.340
Tairetsu’s strong!

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.940
Amazing teamwork...

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:27.890
What is it, Go?

00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:30.670
Is it just me, or is there something off
about that Tairetsu?

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:31.280
Huh?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.330
You’re right.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.150
They’re not moving as one.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:48.940
Maybe the team
hasn’t been together for long...

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:54.340
Sarunori!

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.890
Don’t do that, Sarunori!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.440
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.120
Satoshi! You look after the rest!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.670
Got it!

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:28.440
Oh, there!

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.440
Sorry about that.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:31.910
That leaves...

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.260
Okay, just wait there!

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.680
Stop!

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.130
Barely caught it.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.620
What’s that?

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.840
Oh, sorry...

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.880
Satoshi and Pikachu
hit you too hard...

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.690
You weren’t used to
battling yet, huh?

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:24.220
The others must be worried,
so let’s head back!

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.030
What’s wrong?

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:35.550
Are you feeling depressed
because you couldn’t fight properly?

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.260
Well, that happens,
doesn’t it?

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:42.690
You’ve only just
become a team, right?

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:45.370
You just have to practice, yeah?

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.130
One, two, three, four, five...

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.210
Okay, they’re all here.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:00.830
Settle down.

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:03.330
Go’s looking for your captain.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:17.110
What’s going on now?!

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:18.610
Stop!

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:21.110
Just hold on, Pikachu.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:23.400
Now, break it up...

00:11:24.190 --> 00:11:26.050
I said break it up...

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:26.930
Hey!

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:29.470
Come on...!

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:39.160
What am I supposed
to do with you?!

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:15.320
Pocket Monsters!

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.140
Hey, let’s head back.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.100
It’s the six of you together
that make a Tairetsu, right?

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:41.960
So basically,
you need to be clearer with your orders.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:44.990
I know!

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:48.490
Aceburn, Raichu,
Baope, Hiyape, come on out!

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:55.820
And can you
help us out too, Sarunori?

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:03.890
Show it how you
lead a team, Aceburn.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.370
Huh...?

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.530
That wasn’t supposed to happen...

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.530
They can get along,
and work together, really...

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.800
Better to just
dive right in and try it.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:58.460
You ready?

00:13:58.460 --> 00:14:00.300
We’ll practice giving orders!

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.940
Don’t worry. You can do it!

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.880
It just comes down to practice.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.220
Just be confident
and give them your orders.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:25.360
Trust that everyone
will follow you!

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.470
Just give it a go!

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:52.430
Okay, that’s it!
You’re doing great!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.390
Seeing them like this,
it’s like Pikachu’s become their captain.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:02.080
Sorry, sorry...

00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.890
Go’s been a while...

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.030
Yeah. You’ve got it!

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:15.560
Be confident,
and trust that they’ll follow you!

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:25.730
Now you just need to try it
with the troopers!

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.320
Satoshi!

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:46.460
Go!

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.260
Did you find the captain?

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:51.360
Huh?

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:52.510
What’re they doing?

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:56.670
I had them help
with a little training.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.660
Huh? Pikachu?

00:16:01.720 --> 00:16:04.650
These guys won’t
leave Pikachu alone...

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.030
With the captain missing,

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:10.030
I guess they panicked and
stuck to the nearest Pokémon, Pikachu.

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.380
Go on, captain!

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:32.220
Whoa! They’re doing it!

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:33.090
You could say that.

00:16:40.490 --> 00:16:42.850
<i>You</i> don’t have to
stick to anyone.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.580
What do ya know?
They’re better than before.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.710
Right? They’re nearly there.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.160
What?!

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.270
Who’s that Pokémon?

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.870
Koorippo! Penguin Pokémon!
Ice type!

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:32.300
It drifted in on the flow of ocean waters
from a frigid place!

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:35.270
It keeps its head iced constantly
to keep it cold!

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:37.030
I wonder if it’s lost.

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.880
Looks like they’re gonna battle!

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:47.450
Perfect!
Experience is the best teacher!

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:50.290
Go for it!

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:54.800
All right!

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.100
You’ve got it!

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:32.340
Whoa, they’re in perfect sync!

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:44.850
They’re fortifying their defenses with Protect!
That’s a great decision!

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:59.180
The ice...!

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:09.160
Ooh... So that’s what its face
looked like inside that.

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:16.980
It ran off.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:22.200
Whoa, you really were acting
like one Pokémon!

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:25.110
And that is a true Tairetsu!

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:26.140
Great work!

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:33.170
Yeah. Keep working together
as a team now, okay?

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.010
Okay, we’ve got our data
on Tairetsu.

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:39.520
Let’s head back, then.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.810
What’re they doing?

00:20:13.760 --> 00:20:14.620
Huh?

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:17.220
I think they’re saying
they wanna come with you.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.350
Really?

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:22.360
Okay!

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.660
Monster Ball, go!

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.170
Tairetsu’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:39.790
I caught a Tairetsu!

00:20:42.280 --> 00:20:44.430
Thanks for all the help,
all of you!

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:47.600
Galar’s really a fun place!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:51.400
I get stoked just thinking about
all the Pokémon here I haven’t seen yet!

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:53.270
Let’s come back here
for more research!

00:20:57.090 --> 00:21:00.130
Go has caught new Pokémon
in the Galar Region.

00:21:01.470 --> 00:21:04.530
But... What happened
to that Koorippo?

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:09.660
Now, for our next adventure!

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:10.860
Go!

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:15.370
People are suffering
from nightmares in Sinnoh?!

00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:17.410
Let’s check it out, Go!

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:17.910
What?!

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:19.410
Our family vacation’s canceled?!

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:21.830
Then... We should go on our own.

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:24.440
But I’m a bit worried...

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:26.480
It’ll be fine, it’ll be fine!

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:27.340
Who are you?

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:28.300
Let’s go together!

00:23:29.890 --> 00:23:31.730
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.730 --> 00:23:34.360
Darkrai: A Midsummer Night’s Dream
